guamp: shader priming replays the journal on every boot of the same build too (warm) and keeps the states it makes alive

fin53 (live-20261106-092610, warm cache "V cache hit112 miss0"): the render server still made each pipeline on its render thread at its
first draw: T pipeline n=112 total=1471 ms max=154 ms; 59 of them between 31 and 91 s of the boot in 869 ms (14.7 ms each), then about
7 ms each (vkpipe 2.5 ms of it). 0046 skips the replay once prime-replay-done lists the build. Now a boot whose build was replayed
replays the 128 most frequent descriptors 10 s after the device opened (one quiet wait first, cache hits at background QoS), and both
replays keep up to 128 states alive, so CoreAnimation's own creation shares the live variant (shader modules, layouts, VkPipelines:
metal2vulkan-runtime pipeline/memo.rs) instead of reading the disk cache and calling the driver on its render thread. The journal's
lines of the priming thread itself (callers "qc global=..." without QuartzCore frames) no longer count. NMB_PRIME_WARM=0 and
NMB_PRIME_HOLD=0 turn the two off; prime.log gets "warm lines=.. made=.. held=.. ms=..". Host check: clang -fsyntax-only -fobjc-arc as
Objective-C++ against stand-in Foundation/Metal headers. Applies after 0046.

